{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Who seats the barren woman</b> — in the pattern of גברת; and the word is not in construct to \"house.\" He seats the barren woman, and she dwells in a house, like \"who seats the solitary woman in a home,\" and \"house\" as in: בית אהרן, בית יעקב, \"a man and his household.\"" "And the sense of \"a mother of children\" — that the barren woman becomes a joyful mother of children, as the words of Hannah: \"for I rejoice in Your deliverance.\" And the poet concludes with the word Hallelujah, upon these wonders that HaShem does."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 113, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:36.080440940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}